                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 153.]</seg></opener>
                <p>William Wegmer was born at Schützingen, Würtemberg, December 20, 1868, and
                    emigrated in 1884 to the United States, where he became naturalized as an
                    American citizen on October 21, 1891, at Newark, N. J., where he now resides. In
                    1892 an attachment was placed upon an inheritance coming to him for his failure
                    to perform military service. Upon intervention made in his behalf under date of
                    June 3, 1893, the attachment was removed and instructions were given to the
                    state’s attorney to desist from all further prosecution of the case.</p>
            </div>
